# Engineering standards (always)

Before claiming Done, shipping governance-adjacent work, or closing a “looks fixed” bug, follow **`docs/ENGINEERING_STANDARDS.md`**:

1. **Evidence-linked PASS** — prod trace/audit/HTTP artifact, not pytest alone.
2. **One layer ≠ done** — confirm every user-facing layer (API + UI + deploy).
3. **Dual paths** — ReAct vs governed chat (etc.) need independent verification until they share one gate.
4. **Schema-gate ≠ authorization** — PII / third-party ML purpose needs a named owner + written option (see STA-312 / Memory Option B).
5. **Class-level** — check structural/shared-path bugs before closing an isolated case.

Memory Phase 1 caveat: opaque-alias vectors are **exact HMAC match** of normalized mentions — not fuzzy `"Sarah"`↔`"Sarah Smith"`.
